      "cambodia/khmer-rouge-history": {
        "name": "Tuol Sleng and the Killing Fields",
        "description": "Memorials to the victims of the Khmer Rouge regime, a sobering but important visit.",
        "details": "Tuol Sleng (S-21) was a school turned prison and now a genocide museum, and Choeung Ek is a mass-grave site outside the city with an audio guide. The visits are harrowing, so allow a quiet evening afterwards. Dress respectfully, and do not take inappropriate photographs.",
